Hi Tyler,

That's great! FWIW, mlg.custom() will not do anything more than allow
you to keep the MLG assignments stored in the genclone/snpclone object
so that you can subset them without worry.

On 4/12/20 3:16 PM, Tyler Smith wrote:
> Hi Zhian,
>
> Thanks, that's basically what I ended up doing. I wrote a short script
> that checked each sample with incomplete data:
>
> - IF `mlg` hadn't already matched it to a complete genotype from  its
> own population
> - AND it had a 0 distance (from diss.dist) with a complete mlg in  its
> own population
> - THEN reassign the incomplete genotype to a matching complete mlg  in
> its own population
>
> I didn't use `mll.custom`, although I should look into that, it might
> be more straightforward. In any case, once I had a corrected mlg
> vector, it was straightforward to get the stats I want from `table`
> and `vegan::rarify`.
